 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Dominated by the projection step (optimization) and supplementary sampling. At resolution $N=256$, projection takes 5984 ms, supplementary sampling takes 1566 ms, and thinning takes 519 ms [S1]. The V2M lookup table step takes 107 ms [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Dominated by the projection step (optimization) and supplementary sampling [S1]. At resolution $N=256$, projection takes 5984 ms, supplementary sampling takes 1566 ms, and thinning takes 519 ms [S1]. The V2M lookup table step takes 107 ms [S1].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Proportional to the grid resolution $N^3$ for storing the UDF and active voxel grid [G].
 *   **Performance:** DCx produces meshes with higher accuracy and robustness than existing methods (DCUDF, NDC, DMUDF) on both manifold and non-manifold inputs [S1]. It avoids the double-layer entanglement of DCUDF and the multi-layer artifacts of NDC/DMUDF [S1].
